# A stored name outside the printable-ASCII domain, legally sealed. The
# medium can carry one — whatever wrote it need not have been this library
# — and enumeration must report the bytes as they are rather than filter
# them through the port's string type. Rendering the name through a &str
# once turned it into nothing at all, and the comparison driver could not
# even decode the C runner's output (#119).
init zeros 8192
format 4
add a 00
poke 256 80
reseal 256
list
read a 8192
